          equipment: 'Cards plus a score track for penalty points.',
          dealing: "Deal 4 cards to each player. Leader is player to dealer's left.",
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid penalty points by winning the fourth (last) trick, or by staying out of expensive losing positions after knocks.',
          gameplay: '1. **Deal**: Four cards each from a 32-card deck. 2. **Play**: Four tricks are played; players follow suit when able, otherwise discard any card. 3. **Trick winner**: Highest card of the led suit wins and leads next. 4. **Knocking**: After players pick up cards, and at any time during the hand, a player may knock to raise the stake by one life. 5. **Fold or stay**: Opponents may fold (take current loss) or continue. 6. **Hand result**: Winner of trick four avoids loss; others who stayed lose according to the raised stake. 7. **Elimination**: In Siwweschroom, players reaching seven penalty points drop out; last survivor wins.',
          keyRules: [
            'No trumps are used.',
            'Only the last trick decides the hand winner.',
            'Knocks raise risk for everyone still in.',
            'A player cannot knock and then fold to that same knock.',
            'Siwweschroom end condition is elimination at 7 points, not a fixed 10-point loser rule.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Preserve your strongest suit card for trick four whenever possible; early tricks are mainly about control of the final lead.',
          intermediate: 'Use folds proactively: conceding one stake is often better than staying into a bad final trick under raised stakes.',
          advanced: 'Time knocks around information edges, such as after seeing opponents commit high cards in a suit you can still dominate on trick four.',
          tips: [
            'Track who can still follow each suit by trick three.',
            'If you cannot realistically win trick four, fold early before another knock lands.',
            'When near elimination, avoid speculative knocks and prioritize survival.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
